   "Halcyon-researcher": "accommodating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "collaborating"
  },
  "section_notes": "The final S2 ceiling of 7.5% with investigation only above 5% lets Northwind's 6.2% failure rate pass without a fail, while Halcyon's stricter 2.1% is no advantage. S3's 7-year retrofit window and S4's 36-month suppression deadline with equivalent-measure options both relieve Northwind's higher retrofit burden and cost, and S5 stays flexible on recall and disclosure triggers. S1's strict 24-hour and 5-day reporting still exposes both companies' unreported incidents, which is the main public-protection gain."
